&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring an experienced full stack engineer to help small businesses work better with AI. You&#39;ll build Gus, Gusto&#39;s AI-powered assistant, and create scalable solutions that serve millions of users. As a Software Engineer at this level, you&#39;ll own projects end-to-end from initial specs to deployed features—working at the intersection of modern AI capabilities and real business needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Core Experience - AI Experiences team owns Gus, Gusto&#39;s AI-powered assistant, and the platform that enables teams across Gusto to deliver AI-native experiences to customers across web, mobile, voice, email, and agent-based channels. You&#39;ll work within Gusto&#39;s AI platform infrastructure, collaborating closely with sister teams who own the underlying agent framework. Your focus is building experiences and enabling product teams to extend and scale within the platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This work is directly tied to Gusto&#39;s top priorities. We operate with fast iteration cycles, deep cross-functional collaboration, and high ownership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here&#39;s what you&#39;ll do day-to-day:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect, build, and test technologies supporting AI experiences within Gusto&#39;s product suite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create standardized, self-serve patterns that enable product teams to extend Gus across web, voice, email, and agent-based experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with ML and product teams on prompt engineering, clarifying question flows, and escalation logic—using A/B tests and data to drive improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers on complex technical challenges in AI, scalability, and platform infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help scale a large Ruby/Rails and React application serving millions of users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product, Design, Security, and Technical Operations teams to understand customer needs, develop solutions, and launch features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build customer-facing products end-to-end that customers rely on every day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here&#39;s what we&#39;re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of software development experience, with 4+ years building scalable platforms or high-impact customer-facing products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong foundation in front-end engineering and modern web technologies (Ruby on Rails, React, GraphQL, or similar full-stack frameworks) with ability to build well-structured, maintainable code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of owning multi-quarter projects that solve complex engineering problems and deliver measurable customer impact at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building internal platforms or developer-facing infrastructure that enables other teams to self-serve and ship AI-powered features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent cross-functional communication skills with ability to mentor engineers and collaborate effectively across teams and stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product-minded, customer-facing engineering approach with passion for creating great customer experiences and ownership over performance, reliability, and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus if you have AI platform development experience or strong learning orientation toward AI technologies, patterns, and frameworks (orchestration, evals, prompt systems—not ML model development)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our cash compensation amount for this role is targeted at $163,000-$204,000 in Denver, $178,000-$223,000 for Los Angeles and most remote locations, $197,000-$247,000 for San Francisco, New York, and Seattle. Final offer amounts are determined by multiple factors including candidate experience, level, and expertise and may vary from the amounts listed above.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
